{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Now I understand the process. I need to:\n1. Create build scripts for both CSV files under `.xorq/scripts/`\n2. Build them with `xorq build`\n3. Add them to the catalog with `xorq catalog add` - ONE AT A TIME\n4. Then compute the metric (farmers markets per 100,000 residents)\n5. Verify with xorq_verify\n\nFor the farmers markets CSV, I just need to sum up all the farmers markets (excluding territories).\n\nFor the population, I need to read the census file and get the 2025 population for the 'United States' row.\n\nThen I'll create a metric that calculates the ratio and verifies it.\n\nLet me start by creating the build scripts and then build them."}}
